course: dictionary
lesson: 9114
title: Reading a smile
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A smile is when your mouth curves up at the ends, often showing your teeth. To smile means to make that shape, usually because you are happy, friendly or amused.
explain: A smile can tell you more than the word itself. «Maya smiled, but her eyes stayed sad.» The smile is there, but the sad eyes show she is hiding a sad feeling. So a smile does not always mean someone is truly happy.
explain: Look at the words around the smile to understand it. «He gave a warm smile and held the door open.» Warm tells you the smile was kind and friendly, and holding the door open backs that up.
fact: A smile is the happy look on your face, and to smile means to make that look.
fact: «Smile» is a noun in «a big smile» and a verb in «she smiled».
fact: «Warm» smile means kind and friendly; other smiles can be shy, sly or nervous.
fact: A smile does not always mean someone is truly happy or kind.
fact: Useful phrases: «smile back» means return a smile, and «put a smile on someone's face» means make someone happy.
exercise: «Hamid is fed up, but he smiles.» What does smiles mean here? | *Makes his mouth curve up at the ends | Falls fast asleep | Runs out of the room | Shouts loudly at the aunties
exercise: «She gave a big smile.» Which word is the noun, the happy look on her face? | big | gave | she | *smile
exercise: «Maya smiled, but her eyes stayed sad.» Why might Maya's smile not mean she is happy? | *She is hiding a sad feeling behind her smile | She is too tired to smile | Her eyes are closed | Smiling always means happy
test: What does «put a smile on someone's face» mean? | Draw a face on a card | Hide a smile | Make someone cross | *Make someone happy
test: Which smile is a warm smile? | A sleepy smile | A hidden smile under a hat | *A kind and friendly smile | An angry, loud smile
exam: People all over the world understand a smile, but what is true about it? | *It does not always mean someone is truly happy or kind | Only children can smile | It only means the person is angry | It means the person is asleep
